            <ArticleTitle>Monitoring in cardiovascular disease patients by nonlinear biomedical signal processing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6564-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1109/IEMBS.2011.6091619</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Due to recent advances in technology extensive cardiovascular monitoring is widely introduced today. An essential component of cardiovascular monitoring is the analysis of several biosignals as electrocardiogram, blood pressure and other vital signs. This manuscript provides an overview about several application fields of cardiovascular monitoring with the main focus on nonlinear dynamics analysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
